-- CONTROL — THE ALIAS MUST NOT POISON THE BARE NAME.  Both declarers reachable,
-- one aliased, but only the bare `Node` is written.  Nothing strips cb's
-- constructor onto the bare key, so this program means exactly what it meant
-- before an alias carried constructors and contributes ZERO rows.  Widening the
-- collision to every bare occurrence of a name some alias could also reach
-- would light this up and reject a program that was always well defined.
import ca.{TA(..)}
import cb as B

x : TA
x = Node 1

useB : B.TB -> Int
useB _ = 0
